# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the SECONDO regression suite.
#
# Every entry below is a REAL leak that was measured, not a false positive.
# They are suppressed so leak detection can stay switched on and still catch
# anything NEW. This list is a ratchet: work it down, do not add to it. When a
# leak is fixed, delete its line and the suite will keep it fixed.
#
# Measured from a full 'run-tests.sh -tty' pass on an ASan build, 2026-08-19.
# Counts are leaked objects observed in that run.
#
# LSan matches each pattern as a substring of the symbolised frame, so an entry
# also hides future leaks from the same function. Entries marked BROAD name a
# core engine entry point shared by unrelated callers -- those blind the most
# and are worth replacing with a real fix first, ahead of raw size.

